                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0130aa39-b329-4844-bcf9-a871c2311e57",
                        "source_entry_id": "367f7781-2e49-3dbb-8e70-1630e13db28e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d7b8189-846c-3937-977f-1b54f2978158",
                        "target_lang_word": "foundling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foundling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4fbf2ef-89ab-3557-a5b8-b206c6a455fc",
                                        "entry_id": "cfaa29fc-a168-3aa4-b6b1-9e93bfca5799",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abandoned child, left by its parent(s), often a baby left at a convent or similar safe place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13aaac05-4e4b-4231-9184-5bef41b59ed3",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fbf2ef-89ab-3557-a5b8-b206c6a455fc",
                                                "text": "foundling hospital"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06ce5bd2-8b38-4fb9-bcc0-55ace20d7608",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fbf2ef-89ab-3557-a5b8-b206c6a455fc",
                                                "text": "In foundling hospitals, and among the children brought up by parish charities, the mortality is still greater than among those of the common people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34c35c4b-b78a-4b9c-8250-4e23f4bb9bc4",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fbf2ef-89ab-3557-a5b8-b206c6a455fc",
                                                "text": "Moses was a foundling; Jesus Christ was born in a stable; and Mahomet was a mule driver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fb6dd8e-0444-4c2f-a186-6e43a76394b1",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fbf2ef-89ab-3557-a5b8-b206c6a455fc",
                                                "text": "[Owl:] YOU HEARD THAT FREMOUNT IS REALLY A^([sic]) ANT LION, MR. CONGERSMAN?\n [Frog:] IT'S A SAD BLOW TO THE PARTY JUST AT A TIME WHEN US OWLS MUST STICK TOGETHER. WORST PART IS, MRS. WEEVIL SAYS HER SISTER-AN'-LAW FOUND THE CANDIDATE IN A BOX OF POPCORN.\n [Owl:] AIN'T IT WORSE TO BE A CANNIBAL THAN A FOUNDLING?\n [Frog:] WE CAN SAY HE'S CHANGED HIS HABITS! BUT A FAMILY TREE LOOKS BAD SPROUTIN' OUT OF POPCORN⋯"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c933d75-c20d-4a4f-94e9-943e25be264f",
                        "source_entry_id": "367f7781-2e49-3dbb-8e70-1630e13db28e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d7b8189-846c-3937-977f-1b54f2978158",
                        "target_lang_word": "nalezenec",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nalezenec",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3beaaf17-6f03-304f-8219-d3dcd364f419",
                                        "entry_id": "b23d2381-6776-38da-a387-1344e2207065",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "dítě, které rodiče odložili v úmyslu vzdát se ho (a bylo nalezeno); nalezené dítě"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e75f2496-ba5f-3f4d-b176-509b4d978e4e",
                                        "entry_id": "b23d2381-6776-38da-a387-1344e2207065",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ten, kdo byl ztracený a našel se"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2fb7f3f-e55e-4285-a3c6-4e335fb57ae0",
                                                "sense_id": "e75f2496-ba5f-3f4d-b176-509b4d978e4e",
                                                "text": "„Poslušně hlásím,“ ozval se dobrácký hlas Švejkův, „že jsem zde v garnizónu jako nalezenec.“"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5ffa2dc6-b7cd-4278-a3cc-037a2a2bda16",
                        "source_entry_id": "367f7781-2e49-3dbb-8e70-1630e13db28e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d7b8189-846c-3937-977f-1b54f2978158",
                        "target_lang_word": "enfant trouvé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "enfant trouvé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7709b40-9cfd-3083-8ce9-081630276727",
                                        "entry_id": "236be239-2fc1-3407-bdf0-fe3cae5f22c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bébé abandonné par sa mère en un lieu quelconque et recueilli par une âme charitable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Famille"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff900a78-d8ed-4e01-a9b2-bc655bb45b40",
                                                "sense_id": "c7709b40-9cfd-3083-8ce9-081630276727",
                                                "text": "Je suis un enfant trouvé.\nMais jusqu’à huit ans j’ai cru que, comme tous les autres enfants, j’avais une mère, car lorsque je pleurais, il y avait une femme qui me serrait si doucement dans ses bras, en me berçant, que mes larmes s’arrêtaient de couler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df59e324-aabf-4241-a97b-cb0dbeab33fa",
                                                "sense_id": "c7709b40-9cfd-3083-8ce9-081630276727",
                                                "text": "Je parlai de mes parents sans dire qu’ils n’étaient pas réellement mes père et mère, car il aurait fallu avouer en même temps que je n’étais qu’un enfant trouvé ; et c’était là une honte à laquelle je ne pouvais pas me résigner tant j’avais souffert, depuis que je me rendais compte de mes sensations, du mépris que j’avais vu, dans notre village, marquer en toutes occasions aux enfants des hospices : enfant trouvé ! il me semblait que c’était tout ce qu’il y avait de plus abject au monde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "edf761e0-8ba2-4035-8b58-2bf0fc0ed683",
                        "source_entry_id": "367f7781-2e49-3dbb-8e70-1630e13db28e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d7b8189-846c-3937-977f-1b54f2978158",
